// Title: Winnti Pipemon Characteristics
// Sigma ID: 73d70463-75c9-4258-92c6-17500fe972f2
// Status: stable | Level: critical
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), oscd.community
// Date: 2020-07-30 | Modified: 2021-11-27
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, execution, stealth, T1574.001, G0044
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects specific process characteristics of Winnti Pipemon malware reported by ESET
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate setups that use similar flags
// References:
//   - https://www.welivesecurity.com/2020/05/21/no-game-over-winnti-group/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules-emerging-threats/2020/TA/Winnti/proc_creation_win_apt_winnti_pipemon.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "setup0.exe -p" or (ProcessCommandLine contains "setup.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine endswith "-x:0" or ProcessCommandLine endswith "-x:1" or ProcessCommandLine endswith "-x:2"))
